WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.710
- Quentin Tarantino and Miramax

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.570
have reached a settlement over the lawsuit

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.630
regarding Tarantino's attempt to make NFTs

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.310
from the movie "Pulp Fiction"

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.010
to which Miramax owns a lot of the rights.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:11.843
If you don't recall,

00:00:11.843 --> 00:00:12.870
Miramax claimed that Tarantino

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.390
was infringing Miramax's copyrights

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.580
over the movie "Pulp Fiction"

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.540
when he planned to create
NFTs based on certain portions

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.850
of the script to the movie itself.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.440
It's a shame that we'll
probably never learn

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.330
the actual outcome of this suit.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.280
There were arguments on both sides.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.740
Miramax owned the right
to the movie itself,

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.740
but Tarantino probably had a good argument

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.460
that he owned the rights to
his handwritten screenplays.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.670
Where an NFT falls on
that spectrum, who knows,

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.220
but it would be interesting
to have actual case law

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.053
on that suit.

00:00:45.053 --> 00:00:47.340
And while we won't know who
won or lost this lawsuit,

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.470
we do know that there
is a true loser here.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.540
It's the person that bought
Tarantino's first NFT

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.803
for $1.1 million.

